# TypeScript & React Native Development Standards

## 🎯 Code Quality Standards

### TypeScript Configuration
- **Strict mode enabled**: Follow the strict TypeScript settings in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json)
- **No implicit any**: Explicit typing required
- **Unused imports**: Must be removed (`noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`)
- **Null safety**: Strict null checks enabled

### Import/Export Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Use explicit exports from package index
export { default as MobileCore } from './MobileCore';
export { LogLevel } from './models/LogLevel';

// ✅ Named imports preferred
import { LogLevel } from './models/LogLevel';
import MobileCore from './MobileCore';

// ❌ Avoid default exports for utilities
```

### Type Definitions
```typescript
// ✅ Define interfaces for all public APIs
export interface VisitorID {
  idOrigin: string;
  idType: string;
  id: string;
  authenticationState: MobileVisitorAuthenticationState;
}

// ✅ Use enums for constants
export enum LogLevel {
  ERROR = 'AEP_LOG_LEVEL_ERROR',
  WARNING = 'AEP_LOG_LEVEL_WARNING',
  DEBUG = 'AEP_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG',
  VERBOSE = 'AEP_LOG_LEVEL_VERBOSE'
}
```

## 📱 React Native Patterns

### Native Module Integration
- Always use `NativeModules` from React Native
- Implement proper error handling for native calls
- Use Promise-based APIs consistently

### Component Structure
```typescript
// ✅ Functional components with proper typing
interface Props {
  title: string;
  onPress?: () => void;
}

const MyComponent: React.FC<Props> = ({ title, onPress }) => {
  // Implementation
};
```

## 📄 File Headers
All source files must include the Adobe license header:
```typescript
/*
Copyright 2022 Adobe. All rights reserved.
This file is licensed to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
*/
```

## 🧪 Testing Patterns
- Test files should be in `__tests__/` directories
- Use descriptive test names
- Mock native modules when necessary
- Follow the Jest configuration in [jest.config.js](mdc:jest.config.js)
